{"title": "Sectional Mock #69 (Mixed)", "duration_min": 30.0, "questions": [{"q_en": "<p>If the total surface area of the hemisphere is 13975.5 cm<sup>2</sup>, then find the diameter of the hemisphere. </p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 13975.5 cm<sup>2</sup> &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2343;&#2327;&#2379;&#2354;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2360; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["55 cm", "81 cm", "77 cm", "62 cm"], "options_hi": ["55 cm", "81 cm", "77 cm", "62 cm"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>The total surface area of the hemisphere = 3&#960;r<sup>2</sup></p><p>13975.5 = 3 * 22/7 * r<sup>2</sup></p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 1482.25 </p><p>r = 38.5 cm</p><p>Hence, the diameter of the hemisphere = 2 * 38.5</p><p>= 77 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>The total surface area of the hemisphere = 3&#960;r<sup>2</sup></p><p>13975.5 = 3 * 22/7 * r<sup>2</sup></p><p>r<sup>2</sup> = 1482.25 </p><p>r = 38.5 cm</p><p>Hence, the diameter of the hemisphere = 2 * 38.5</p><p>= 77 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the value of:</p><p><div><div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-</p><p>align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">p<sup>2</sup> - (q - r)<sup>2</sup>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;:</p><p><div><div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-</p><p>align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">p<sup>2</sup> - (q - r)<sup>2</sup>", "options_en": ["1", "2", "0", "3"], "options_hi": ["1", "2", "0", "3"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p><img width=236 height=52 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24263/image054.png\"></p><p><img width=412 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24263/image055.png\"></p><p><img width=225 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24263/image056.png\"></p><p><img width=217 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24263/image057.png\"></p><p><img width=103 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24263/image058.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=236 height=52 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24263/image054.png\"></p><p><img width=412 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24263/image055.png\"></p><p><img width=225 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24263/image056.png\"></p><p><img width=217 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24263/image057.png\"></p><p><img width=103 height=44 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p24263/image058.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>Evaluate:</p><p><div><div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">(232)<sup>3</sup> + (140)<sup>3</sup> + (353)<sup>3</sup> - 3 x 232 x 140 x 353", "q_hi": "<p>&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;  :</p><p><div><div style=\"display: inline-block;position: relative;vertical-align: middle;\"><span style=\"text-align:center;display: block; padding: 0;\">(232)<sup>3</sup> + (140)<sup>3</sup> + (353)<sup>3</sup> - 3 x 232 x 140 x 353", "options_en": ["261", "725", "445", "596"], "options_hi": ["261", "725", "445", "596"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup> + c<sup>3</sup>  -  3abc = (a + b + c)(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>  -  ab  -  bc  -  ca)</p><p>put,</p><p>232 = a, 140 = b, 353 = c in the equation,</p><p>[(232)<sup>3</sup>+(140)<sup>3</sup>+(353)<sup>3</sup> - 3*232*140* 353]/[(232)<sup>2</sup>+(140)<sup>2</sup>+(353)<sup>2</sup> - 232*140 - 140*353  -  353*232]</p><p>=&gt; [(a)<sup>3</sup> + (b)<sup>3</sup> + (c)<sup>3</sup>  -  3abc]/[a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>  -  ab  -  bc  -  ca]</p><p>=&gt; [(a+b+c)(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>  -  ab  -  bc  -  ca)]/[a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>  -  ab  -  bc  -  ca]</p><p>=&gt; a + b + c</p><p>=&gt; 232 + 140 + 353 = 725</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>a<sup>3</sup> + b<sup>3</sup> + c<sup>3</sup>  -  3abc = (a + b + c)(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>  -  ab  -  bc  -  ca)</p><p>put,</p><p>232 = a, 140 = b, 353 = c in the equation,</p><p>[(232)<sup>3</sup>+(140)<sup>3</sup>+(353)<sup>3</sup> - 3*232*140* 353]/[(232)<sup>2</sup>+(140)<sup>2</sup>+(353)<sup>2</sup> - 232*140 - 140*353  -  353*232]</p><p>=&gt; [(a)<sup>3</sup> + (b)<sup>3</sup> + (c)<sup>3</sup>  -  3abc]/[a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>  -  ab  -  bc  -  ca]</p><p>=&gt; [(a+b+c)(a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>  -  ab  -  bc  -  ca)]/[a<sup>2</sup> + b<sup>2</sup> + c<sup>2</sup>  -  ab  -  bc  -  ca]</p><p>=&gt; a + b + c</p><p>=&gt; 232 + 140 + 353 = 725</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a trapezium PQRS, PQ II SR and SR = 18.6 cm. If PQ &gt; SR and the length of the line segment joining the mid-points of its diagonals is 4.8 cm, then find the value of PQ.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2354;&#2306;&#2348; PQRS &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, PQ II SR &#2324;&#2352; SR = 18.6 cm &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; PQ &gt; SR &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2357;&#2367;&#2325;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2350;&#2343;&#2381;&#2351;-&#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2344;&#2375; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2352;&#2375;&#2326;&#2366;&#2326;&#2306;&#2337; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 4.8 cm &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; PQ &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2351;&#2375;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["28.2 cm", "24.8 cm", "32.4 cm", "36.6 cm"], "options_hi": ["28.2 cm", "24.8 cm", "32.4 cm", "36.6 cm"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>According to the question:</p><p><img width=246 height=157 id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8274/image001.png\"></p><p>As we know, length of the line segment joining the mid-points of diagonals of trapezium PQRS = 4.8cm</p><p>= AB</p><p>= (PQ  -  SR)/2</p><p>Then, 4.8 = (PQ  -  18.6)/2</p><p><b>PQ = 28.2 cm</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>According to the question:</p><p><img width=246 height=157 id=\"Picture 1\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p8274/image001.png\"></p><p>As we know, length of the line segment joining the mid-points of diagonals of trapezium PQRS = 4.8cm</p><p>= AB</p><p>= (PQ  -  SR)/2</p><p>Then, 4.8 = (PQ  -  18.6)/2</p><p><b>PQ = 28.2 cm</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>A gives B and C both a start of 40 m however. A and B finished the race at the same time while C is 10 m away from the finishing point. How much start B gives C if the length of race course is 1200 m?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>A, B &#2324;&#2352; C &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2379; 40 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2325;&#2368; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2310;&#2340; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; A &#2324;&#2352; B &#2344;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2361;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2342;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364; &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2348;&#2325;&#2367; C &#2309;&#2306;&#2340;&#2367;&#2350; &#2348;&#2367;&#2306;&#2342;&#2369; &#2360;&#2375; 10 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2342;&#2370;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2352;&#2375;&#2360; &#2325;&#2379;&#2352;&#2381;&#2360; &#2325;&#2368; &#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312; 1200 &#2350;&#2368;&#2335;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2379; B, C &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2368; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2369;&#2310;&#2340; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["10(10/29) m", "10(8/29) m", "9(10/29) m", "10(9/29) m"], "options_hi": ["10(10/29) &#2350;&#2368;", "10(8/29) &#2350;&#2368;", "9(10/29) &#2350;&#2368;", "10(9/29) &#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>When A covers 1200 m </p><p>=&gt; B covers 1200  -  40 = 1160 m</p><p>C is 10 m away from the finishing point</p><p>=&gt; B gives C a start of =&gt; 10/1160 * 1200 = 300/29 = 10(10/29) m</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>When A covers 1200 m </p><p>=&gt; B covers 1200  -  40 = 1160 m</p><p>C is 10 m away from the finishing point</p><p>=&gt; B gives C a start of =&gt; 10/1160 * 1200 = 300/29 = 10(10/29) m</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>Simplify:</p><p>(&#8731; [&#8731; 343])<sup>3</sup> x (&#8731; [&#8731; 216])<sup>3</sup></p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2360;&#2352;&#2354;&#2368;&#2325;&#2371;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;:</p><p>(&#8731; [&#8731; 343])<sup>3</sup> x (&#8731; [&#8731; 216])<sup>3</sup></p>", "options_en": ["56", "42", "&#8731;42", "42<sup>3</sup>"], "options_hi": ["56", "42", "&#8731;42", "42<sup>3</sup>"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p><img width=140 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p28447/image008.png\"></p><p><img width=97 height=33 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p28447/image009.png\"></p><p>= 7  X  6</p><p>= 42</p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=140 height=39 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p28447/image008.png\"></p><p><img width=97 height=33 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p28447/image009.png\"></p><p>= 7  X  6</p><p>= 42</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simplification"}, {"q_en": "<p>Bhuvan travels at the speed of 35 km/h by car in 2.4 hours and 12 km/h on foot in 36 minutes. Find his average speed.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2349;&#2369;&#2357;&#2344; 35 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2360;&#2375; 2.4 &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; 12 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366; &#2325;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2360;&#2375; &#2346;&#2376;&#2342;&#2354; 36 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2351;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["26.4 km/h", "29.5 km/h", "32.1 km/h", "30.4 km/h"], "options_hi": ["26.4 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "29.5 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "32.1 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;", "30.4 &#2325;&#2367;&#2350;&#2368;/&#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2366;"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Distance travelled by Bhuvan by car = 35*2.4 = 84 km</p><p>Distance travelled by Bhuvan on foot = 12*36/60 = 7.2 km</p><p>Average speed = (84 + 7.2)/(2.4 + 0.6) = 91.2/3 = 30.4 km/h</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Distance travelled by Bhuvan by car = 35*2.4 = 84 km</p><p>Distance travelled by Bhuvan on foot = 12*36/60 = 7.2 km</p><p>Average speed = (84 + 7.2)/(2.4 + 0.6) = 91.2/3 = 30.4 km/h</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Time, Speed & Distance"}, {"q_en": "<p>LCM and HCF of three numbers 28, 36, and 48 are x and y, respectively, then x is how many times of y?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2340;&#2368;&#2344; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; 28, 36 &#2324;&#2352; 48 &#2325;&#2375; LCM &#2324;&#2352; HCF &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; x &#2324;&#2352; y &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; x, y &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2366; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["252", "126", "378", "63"], "options_hi": ["252", "126", "378", "63"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>LCM of 28, 36, 48 = x = 1008</p><p>HCF of 28, 36, 48 = y = 4</p><p>So, x/y = 1008/4 = 252</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>LCM of 28, 36, 48 = x = 1008</p><p>HCF of 28, 36, 48 = y = 4</p><p>So, x/y = 1008/4 = 252</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>If cos&#8308;&#952; - sin&#8308;&#952; = 4/5, then find the value of sin4&#952;.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; cos&#8308;&#952; - sin&#8308;&#952; = 4/5, &#2340;&#2379; sin4&#952; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["24/25", "21/25", "16/25", "18/25"], "options_hi": ["24/25", "21/25", "16/25", "18/25"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>cos&#8308;&#952; - sin&#8308;&#952; = 4/5</p><p>(cos&#178;&#952; - sin&#178;&#952;)(cos&#178;&#952; + sin&#178;&#952;) = 4/5</p><p>Since cos&#178;&#952; + sin&#178;&#952; = 1 and cos&#178;&#952; - sin&#178;&#952; = cos 2&#952; </p><p>cos 2&#952; = 4/5 </p><p>sin&#178; 2&#952; = 1 - cos&#178; 2&#952; </p><p>= 1 - (4/5)&#178; </p><p>= 1 - 16/25 </p><p>= 9/25 </p><p>sin 2&#952; = 3/5 </p><p>sin 4&#952; = 2 * sin 2&#952; * cos 2&#952; = 2 * (3/5) * (4/5) </p><p>sin 4&#952; = 24/25</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>cos&#8308;&#952; - sin&#8308;&#952; = 4/5</p><p>(cos&#178;&#952; - sin&#178;&#952;)(cos&#178;&#952; + sin&#178;&#952;) = 4/5</p><p>Since cos&#178;&#952; + sin&#178;&#952; = 1 and cos&#178;&#952; - sin&#178;&#952; = cos 2&#952; </p><p>cos 2&#952; = 4/5 </p><p>sin&#178; 2&#952; = 1 - cos&#178; 2&#952; </p><p>= 1 - (4/5)&#178; </p><p>= 1 - 16/25 </p><p>= 9/25 </p><p>sin 2&#952; = 3/5 </p><p>sin 4&#952; = 2 * sin 2&#952; * cos 2&#952; = 2 * (3/5) * (4/5) </p><p>sin 4&#952; = 24/25</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Trigonometry"}, {"q_en": "<p>Which of the following fractions is nearest to 23/31?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2368; &#2349;&#2367;&#2344;&#2381;&#2344; 23/31 &#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2348;&#2360;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2325;&#2335; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["27/39", "15/28", "22/29", "17/22"], "options_hi": ["27/39", "15/28", "22/29", "17/22"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>21/25 = 0.84, 18/23 = 0.78, 16/21 = 0.76, 20/27= 0.74</p><p>Hence, ascending order = 20/27 &lt; 16/21 &lt; 18/23 &lt; 21/25</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>21/25 = 0.84, 18/23 = 0.78, 16/21 = 0.76, 20/27= 0.74</p><p>Hence, ascending order = 20/27 &lt; 16/21 &lt; 18/23 &lt; 21/25</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Number System"}, {"q_en": "<p>What is the sum of first 24 terms of 2 + 4 + 4 + 7 + 8 + 10 + 16 + 13 + ....?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>2 + 4 + 4 + 7 + 8 + 10 + 16 + 13 + .... &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2361;&#2354;&#2375; 24 &#2346;&#2342;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2351;&#2379;&#2327; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["8046", "8176", "8436", "8686"], "options_hi": ["8046", "8176", "8436", "8686"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let S = (2 + 4 + 4 + 7 + 8 + 10 + 16 + 13 + ....)</p><p>Given series is a combination of A.P and G.P. and,</p><p>Sum of first 24 terms = sum of first 12 terms of G.P + sum of first 12 terms of A.P</p><p>Series in G.P = 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + ...</p><p>First term = a = 2</p><p>Common ratio = r = 4/2 = 2</p><p>n = 12</p><p>Then, sum = a(r<sup>n </sup> -  1)/(r  -  1)</p><p>= 2(2<sup>12</sup>  -  1)/(2  -  1)</p><p>= 8190</p><p>Series in A.P = 4 + 7 + 10 + 13 + ...</p><p>First term = a = 4</p><p>Common difference = 7  -  4 = 3</p><p>n = 12</p><p>Then, sum = (n/2)(2a + (n  -  1)d)</p><p>= (12/2)(2 * 4 + (12  -  1)3)</p><p>= 246</p><p>Therefore, sum of first 24 terms = 8190 + 246 = <b>8436</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let S = (2 + 4 + 4 + 7 + 8 + 10 + 16 + 13 + ....)</p><p>Given series is a combination of A.P and G.P. and,</p><p>Sum of first 24 terms = sum of first 12 terms of G.P + sum of first 12 terms of A.P</p><p>Series in G.P = 2 + 4 + 8 + 16 + ...</p><p>First term = a = 2</p><p>Common ratio = r = 4/2 = 2</p><p>n = 12</p><p>Then, sum = a(r<sup>n </sup> -  1)/(r  -  1)</p><p>= 2(2<sup>12</sup>  -  1)/(2  -  1)</p><p>= 8190</p><p>Series in A.P = 4 + 7 + 10 + 13 + ...</p><p>First term = a = 4</p><p>Common difference = 7  -  4 = 3</p><p>n = 12</p><p>Then, sum = (n/2)(2a + (n  -  1)d)</p><p>= (12/2)(2 * 4 + (12  -  1)3)</p><p>= 246</p><p>Therefore, sum of first 24 terms = 8190 + 246 = <b>8436</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>The following table shows the ratio of number of boys to the number of girls in 5 classes.</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Class</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">Ratio of the number of boys to the number of girls</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">A</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">5:6</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">B</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">5:6</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">C</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">3:4</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">D</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">4: 5</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">E</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2:3</td></tr></table><p>If the number of boys in class B is 9 more than the number of boys in class E and the number of girls in class B is 6 more than the number of girls in class E and also the number of girls in class D is equal to the number of boys in class B, then what is the total number of boys in class D?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344;&#2354;&#2367;&#2326;&#2367;&#2340; &#2340;&#2366;&#2354;&#2367;&#2325;&#2366; 5 &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319;, &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2357; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2352;&#2381;&#2358;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404;</p><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse;\"><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366;</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">&#2354;&#2396;&#2325;&#2375; &#2324;&#2352; &#2354;&#2396;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2366; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340;</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">A</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">5:6</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">B</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">5:6</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">C</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">3:4</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">D</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">4: 5</td></tr><tr><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">E</td><td align=\"left\" style=\"border:1px solid black;padding:5px;\">2:3</td></tr></table><p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; E &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; 9 &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; E &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2360;&#2375; 6 &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2341;&#2366; &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; D &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;, &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; B &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2352;&#2366;&#2348;&#2352; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; D &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["26", "30", "28", "20"], "options_hi": ["26", "30", "28", "20"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>Let the number of boys and the number of girls in class B are 5b and 6b respectively.</p><p>Let the number of boys and the number of girls in class E are 2e and 3e respectively.</p><p>We are given,</p><p>5b - 2e = 9.....................(1)</p><p>and 6b -3e =6</p><p>2b-e = 2 .................... (2)</p><p>By solving (1) and (2) we get b =5 and e = 8</p><p>Number of boys in class B =25</p><p>Number of girls in class D = Number of boys in class B = 25</p><p>In class D</p><p>Number of boys : Number of girls = 4 :5</p><p>Number of boys : 25 = 4 :5</p><p>Hence number of boys in class D =20.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the number of boys and the number of girls in class B are 5b and 6b respectively.</p><p>Let the number of boys and the number of girls in class E are 2e and 3e respectively.</p><p>We are given,</p><p>5b - 2e = 9.....................(1)</p><p>and 6b -3e =6</p><p>2b-e = 2 .................... (2)</p><p>By solving (1) and (2) we get b =5 and e = 8</p><p>Number of boys in class B =25</p><p>Number of girls in class D = Number of boys in class B = 25</p><p>In class D</p><p>Number of boys : Number of girls = 4 :5</p><p>Number of boys : 25 = 4 :5</p><p>Hence number of boys in class D =20.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Percentage"}, {"q_en": "<p>The measurement of a wood box is 62  X  34  X  15 cm<sup>3 </sup>(length*width*height). If the thickness of the wood is 0.5 cm then what will be the weight of the box if it is known that weight of 1 cm<sup>3</sup> is 5 gram?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2354;&#2325;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2346; 62 X 34 X 15 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3 </sup>(&#2354;&#2306;&#2348;&#2366;&#2312;*&#2330;&#2380;&#2337;&#2364;&#2366;&#2312;*&#2314;&#2306;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312;) &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2354;&#2325;&#2337;&#2364;&#2368; &#2325;&#2368; &#2350;&#2379;&#2335;&#2366;&#2312; 0.5 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376; &#2340;&#2379; &#2348;&#2325;&#2381;&#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2379;&#2327;&#2366; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2351;&#2361; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2361;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367; 1 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;<sup>3</sup> &#2325;&#2366; &#2357;&#2332;&#2344; 5 &#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["20.82 kg", "17.19 kg", "18.45 kg", "12.62 kg"], "options_hi": ["20.82 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;", "17.19 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;", "18.45 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;", "12.62 &#2325;&#2367;&#2327;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Volume of the wood = External capacity of box  -  Internal capacity of box</p><p>= (62  X  34  X  15)  -  (62  -  1)  X  (34  -  1)  X  (15  -  1)</p><p>= 62  X  34  X  15  -  61  X  33  X  14 = (31620  -  28182) cm<sup>3</sup></p><p>= 3438 cm<sup>3</sup></p><p>Weight of the wood = (3438  X  5) gm = 17190 gm = 17.19 kg</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Volume of the wood = External capacity of box  -  Internal capacity of box</p><p>= (62  X  34  X  15)  -  (62  -  1)  X  (34  -  1)  X  (15  -  1)</p><p>= 62  X  34  X  15  -  61  X  33  X  14 = (31620  -  28182) cm<sup>3</sup></p><p>= 3438 cm<sup>3</sup></p><p>Weight of the wood = (3438  X  5) gm = 17190 gm = 17.19 kg</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (3D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>If A = 6<sup>400</sup>, B = 7<sup>200</sup>, and C = 3<sup>800</sup>, then which of the following is true?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; A = 6<sup>400</sup>, B = 7<sup>200</sup>, &#2324;&#2352; C = 3<sup>800</sup>, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2367;&#2350;&#2381;&#2344; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2360;&#2375; &#2325;&#2380;&#2344; &#2360;&#2366; &#2360;&#2340;&#2381;&#2351; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["A &lt; B &lt; C", "C &lt; A &lt; B", "B &lt; A &lt; C", "A &lt; C &lt; B"], "options_hi": ["A &lt; B &lt; C", "C &lt; A &lt; B", "B &lt; A &lt; C", "A &lt; C &lt; B"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p><img width=177 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image012.png\"></p><p><img width=159 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image013.png\"></p><p><img width=175 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image014.png\"></p><p><img width=136 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image015.png\"></p>", "solution_hi": "<p><img width=177 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image012.png\"></p><p><img width=159 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image013.png\"></p><p><img width=175 height=31 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image014.png\"></p><p><img width=136 height=19 src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p25700/image015.png\"></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>If 1/(x + 4)  -  x = 7, then what is the value of 1/(x + 4)<sup>2</sup> + (x + 4)<sup>2</sup>?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2351;&#2342;&#2367; 1/(x + 4) - x = 7, &#2340;&#2379; 1/(x + 4)<sup>2</sup> + (x + 4)<sup>2</sup> &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2325;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;?</p>", "options_en": ["11", "15", "9", "7"], "options_hi": ["11", "15", "9", "7"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>1/(x + 4)  -  x = 7</p><p>1/(x + 4)  -  (x + 4) = 3</p><p>Squaring both sides  -  </p><p>1/(x + 4)<sup>2</sup> + (x + 4)<sup>2</sup>  -  2 = 9</p><p>1/(x + 4)<sup>2</sup> + (x + 4)<sup>2</sup> = 11</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>1/(x + 4)  -  x = 7</p><p>1/(x + 4)  -  (x + 4) = 3</p><p>Squaring both sides  -  </p><p>1/(x + 4)<sup>2</sup> + (x + 4)<sup>2</sup>  -  2 = 9</p><p>1/(x + 4)<sup>2</sup> + (x + 4)<sup>2</sup> = 11</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Algebra"}, {"q_en": "<p>P borrowed certain amount from bank at 20% SI for 2 years. At the same time, he lent the same amount to Q at same annual rate of compound interest for 2 years. In the process, P earns &#8377;1000, then find the borrowed amount by P.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>P &#2344;&#2375; &#2348;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2360;&#2375; 2 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; 20% &#2360;&#2366;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2339; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2346;&#2352; &#2325;&#2369;&#2331; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2313;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2368;&#2404; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2346;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; Q &#2325;&#2379; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2330;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2357;&#2371;&#2342;&#2381;&#2343;&#2367; &#2348;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2332; &#2325;&#2368; &#2360;&#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359;&#2367;&#2325; &#2342;&#2352; &#2346;&#2352; 2 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2354;&#2367;&#2319; &#2313;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2342;&#2368;&#2404; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306;, P &#8377;1000 &#2325;&#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; P &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2313;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352; &#2354;&#2368; &#2327;&#2312; &#2343;&#2344;&#2352;&#2366;&#2358;&#2367; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["&#8377;30000", "&#8377;20000", "&#8377;25000", "&#8377;15000"], "options_hi": ["&#8377;30000", "&#8377;20000", "&#8377;25000", "&#8377;15000"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let borrowed amount = 'x'</p><p>Interest amount given by P to bank = (x * 20 * 2)/100 = 0.4x</p><p>Interest amount received by P from Q = x * [1.2<sup>2</sup>  -  1] = 0.44x</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>0.44x  -  0.4x = 1000</p><p>x = 25000</p><p>Hence, borrowed amount by P = &#8377;25000</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let borrowed amount = 'x'</p><p>Interest amount given by P to bank = (x * 20 * 2)/100 = 0.4x</p><p>Interest amount received by P from Q = x * [1.2<sup>2</sup>  -  1] = 0.44x</p><p>According to the question:</p><p>0.44x  -  0.4x = 1000</p><p>x = 25000</p><p>Hence, borrowed amount by P = &#8377;25000</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Simple & Compound Interest"}, {"q_en": "<p>The average weight of X articles is 20 kg. Y number of other articles with an average weight of 30 kg, mixed with them. If the average weight of all the articles is 28 kg, then find X: Y.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>X &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352; 20 kg &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; Y &#2360;&#2306;&#2326;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2344;&#2381;&#2351; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2319;&#2305; &#2332;&#2367;&#2344;&#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352; 30 kg &#2361;&#2376;, &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2350;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2357;&#2360;&#2381;&#2340;&#2369;&#2323;&#2306; &#2325;&#2366; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2349;&#2366;&#2352; 28 kg &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; X: Y &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["1: 8", "8: 1", "1: 4", "4: 1"], "options_hi": ["1: 8", "8: 1", "1: 4", "4: 1"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Total weight of X articles = 20X kg</p><p>Total weight of Y articles = 30Y kg</p><p>According to the question,</p><p>(20X + 30Y)/(X + Y) = 28</p><p>20X + 30Y = 28X + 28Y</p><p>2Y = 8X</p><p>X/Y = 2/8</p><p>X/Y = 1/4 = 1: 4</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Total weight of X articles = 20X kg</p><p>Total weight of Y articles = 30Y kg</p><p>According to the question,</p><p>(20X + 30Y)/(X + Y) = 28</p><p>20X + 30Y = 28X + 28Y</p><p>2Y = 8X</p><p>X/Y = 2/8</p><p>X/Y = 1/4 = 1: 4</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}, {"q_en": "<p>One pipe can fill a tank four times as fast as another pipe. If together the two pipes can fill the tank in 48 minutes, the slower pipe alone will be able to fill the tank in:</p>", "q_hi": "&#2319;&#2325; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; &#2325;&#2367;&#2360;&#2368; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2342;&#2370;&#2360;&#2352;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; &#2360;&#2375; &#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2327;&#2369;&#2344;&#2366; &#2340;&#2375;&#2332;&#2364;&#2368; &#2360;&#2375; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2379;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2325;&#2352; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; 48 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2360;&#2325;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2343;&#2368;&#2350;&#2368; &#2327;&#2340;&#2367; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2366; &#2346;&#2366;&#2311;&#2346; &#2309;&#2325;&#2375;&#2354;&#2375; &#2335;&#2376;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2349;&#2352; &#2346;&#2366;&#2319;&#2327;&#2366;:", "options_en": ["192 minutes", "288 minutes", "240 minutes", "144 minutes"], "options_hi": ["192 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "288 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "240 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;", "144 &#2350;&#2367;&#2344;&#2335;"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let the slower pipe's rate = x and the faster = 4x.</p><p>Together rate = 5x; thus, tank capacity = 48  X  5x = 240x.</p><p>Time for slower pipe = (240x)/x = 240 minutes.</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let the slower pipe's rate = x and the faster = 4x.</p><p>Together rate = 5x; thus, tank capacity = 48  X  5x = 240x.</p><p>Time for slower pipe = (240x)/x = 240 minutes.</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Pipes & Cisterns"}, {"q_en": "<p>Parul began a business with Rs.4500 and was joined afterward by Neha with Rs.5400. If the profits at the end of the year were divided by the ratio of 2: 1. After how much time Neha joined the business?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2346;&#2366;&#2352;&#2369;&#2354; &#2344;&#2375; &#2352;&#2369;.4500 &#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2360;&#2375; &#2319;&#2325; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351; &#2358;&#2369;&#2352;&#2370; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2324;&#2352; &#2313;&#2360;&#2325;&#2375; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2352;&#2369;.5400 &#2325;&#2366; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2325;&#2375; &#2344;&#2375;&#2361;&#2366; &#2349;&#2368; &#2311;&#2360;&#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2358;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2354; &#2361;&#2379; &#2327;&#2312;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2325;&#2379; 2:1 &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2344;&#2369;&#2346;&#2366;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2357;&#2367;&#2349;&#2366;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2332;&#2366;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2344;&#2375;&#2361;&#2366; &#2357;&#2381;&#2351;&#2357;&#2360;&#2366;&#2351; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2351; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2358;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2354; &#2361;&#2369;&#2312;?</p>", "options_en": ["5", "7", "6", "8"], "options_hi": ["5", "7", "6", "8"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Let Neha joined the business for X months.</p><p>profit ratio = 2: 1</p><p>4500 * 12/ (5400 * X) = 2/1</p><p>X = 5</p><p>So, Neha joined after 12 - 5 = 7 months</p><p></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let Neha joined the business for X months.</p><p>profit ratio = 2: 1</p><p>4500 * 12/ (5400 * X) = 2/1</p><p>X = 5</p><p>So, Neha joined after 12 - 5 = 7 months</p><p></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>The base of a right pyramid in an equilateral triangle of side 40&radic;3 cm. If the total surface area of the pyramid is 2940&radic;3 cm2, then find its height.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>40&radic;3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368; &#2349;&#2369;&#2332;&#2366; &#2357;&#2366;&#2354;&#2375; &#2360;&#2350;&#2348;&#2366;&#2361;&#2369; &#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2367;&#2349;&#2369;&#2332; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2350;&#2325;&#2379;&#2339; &#2346;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2337; &#2325;&#2366; &#2310;&#2343;&#2366;&#2352;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2346;&#2367;&#2352;&#2366;&#2350;&#2367;&#2337; &#2325;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2346;&#2371;&#2359;&#2381;&#2336;&#2368;&#2351; &#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2375;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2347;&#2354; 2940&radic;3 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;2 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2311;&#2360;&#2325;&#2368; &#2314;&#2305;&#2330;&#2366;&#2312; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["29 cm", "21 cm", "25 cm", "27 cm"], "options_hi": ["29 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "21 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "25 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;", "27 &#2360;&#2375;&#2350;&#2368;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Inradius of the equilateral triangle = side/2&radic;3 = (40&radic;3)/(2&radic;3)</p><p>= 20 cm</p><p>Slant height (l) = &radic;[h<sup>2</sup> + 400]</p><p>Total surface area = &frac12; * (perimeter of the base * slant height) + Base area</p><p>2940&radic;3 = 1/2 * (3 * 40&radic;3 * &radic;[h<sup>2</sup> + 400]) +&radic;3/4 * (40&radic;3)<sup>2</sup></p><p>2940&radic;3 = 60&radic;3 * &radic;[h<sup>2 </sup>+ 400] + 1200&radic;3</p><p>&radic;[h<sup>2</sup> + 400] = 29</p><p>h2 = 841  -  400 = 441</p><p>h = 21 cm</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Inradius of the equilateral triangle = side/2&radic;3 = (40&radic;3)/(2&radic;3)</p><p>= 20 cm</p><p>Slant height (l) = &radic;[h<sup>2</sup> + 400]</p><p>Total surface area = &frac12; * (perimeter of the base * slant height) + Base area</p><p>2940&radic;3 = 1/2 * (3 * 40&radic;3 * &radic;[h<sup>2</sup> + 400]) +&radic;3/4 * (40&radic;3)<sup>2</sup></p><p>2940&radic;3 = 60&radic;3 * &radic;[h<sup>2 </sup>+ 400] + 1200&radic;3</p><p>&radic;[h<sup>2</sup> + 400] = 29</p><p>h2 = 841  -  400 = 441</p><p>h = 21 cm</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mensuration (2D)"}, {"q_en": "<p>Raghu and Prabhu enter into a partnership such that Raghu invests 20% more than Prabhu. After 8 months from the beginning, Raghu left. If at the end of one-year partnership, total profit earned by them is Rs.7020, then find the share of Raghu in profit.</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2352;&#2328;&#2369; &#2324;&#2352; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2349;&#2369; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2333;&#2375;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2311;&#2360; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2325;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2325;&#2367; &#2352;&#2328;&#2369; &#2360;&#2366;&#2333;&#2375;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2346;&#2381;&#2352;&#2349;&#2369; &#2360;&#2375; 20% &#2309;&#2343;&#2367;&#2325; &#2344;&#2367;&#2357;&#2375;&#2358; &#2325;&#2352;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2310;&#2352;&#2306;&#2349; &#2360;&#2375; 8 &#2350;&#2361;&#2368;&#2344;&#2379;&#2306; &#2348;&#2366;&#2342; &#2352;&#2328;&#2369; &#2360;&#2366;&#2333;&#2375;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2331;&#2379;&#2337;&#2364; &#2342;&#2375;&#2340;&#2366; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2366;&#2333;&#2375;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352;&#2368; &#2325;&#2375; 1 &#2357;&#2352;&#2381;&#2359; &#2325;&#2375; &#2309;&#2306;&#2340; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2313;&#2344;&#2325;&#2375; &#2342;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2352;&#2366; &#2309;&#2352;&#2381;&#2332;&#2367;&#2340; &#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366; &#2327;&#2351;&#2366; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2352;&#2369;. 7020 &#2361;&#2376;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2352;&#2328;&#2369; &#2325;&#2366; &#2361;&#2367;&#2360;&#2381;&#2360;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["Rs.4200", "Rs.3900", "Rs.3120", "Rs.2820"], "options_hi": ["&#2352;&#2369;. 4200", "&#2352;&#2369;. 3900", "&#2352;&#2369;. 3120", "&#2352;&#2369;. 2820"], "answer": 2, "solution_en": "<p>Let Prabhu's investment = a</p><p>Then, Raghu's investment = (100 + 20)% of a = (120/100) * a = 6a/5</p><p>Now, profit ratio, Raghu: Prabhu = [(6a/5) * 8)]: (a * 12)</p><p>= 4: 5</p><p>Total profit earned = Rs.7020</p><p>Therefore, share of Raghu = 7020 * 4/(4 + 5)</p><p>= <b>Rs.3120</b></p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Let Prabhu's investment = a</p><p>Then, Raghu's investment = (100 + 20)% of a = (120/100) * a = 6a/5</p><p>Now, profit ratio, Raghu: Prabhu = [(6a/5) * 8)]: (a * 12)</p><p>= 4: 5</p><p>Total profit earned = Rs.7020</p><p>Therefore, share of Raghu = 7020 * 4/(4 + 5)</p><p>= <b>Rs.3120</b></p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Profit & Loss"}, {"q_en": "<p>Four bells toll once every 8 seconds, 10 seconds, 15 seconds and 27 seconds respectively. If all the bells together toll at 7:00 am, then they will toll together next at -</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2330;&#2366;&#2352; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2325;&#2381;&#2352;&#2350;&#2358;&#2307; &#2361;&#2352; 8 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;, 10 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337;, 15 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2324;&#2352; 27 &#2360;&#2375;&#2325;&#2306;&#2337; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2319;&#2325; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2348;&#2332;&#2340;&#2368; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2360;&#2349;&#2368; &#2328;&#2306;&#2335;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2360;&#2369;&#2348;&#2361; 7:00 &#2348;&#2332;&#2375; &#2348;&#2332;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2357;&#2375; &#2309;&#2327;&#2354;&#2368; &#2348;&#2366;&#2352; &#2319;&#2325; &#2360;&#2366;&#2341; &#2348;&#2332;&#2375;&#2306;&#2327;&#2368; -</p>", "options_en": ["7:18 am", "7.05 am", "7:20 am", "7:15 am"], "options_hi": ["7:18 &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2381;&#2344;", "&#2360;&#2369;&#2348;&#2361; 7.05 &#2348;&#2332;&#2375;", "7:20 &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2381;&#2344;", "7:15 &#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2357;&#2366;&#2361;&#2381;&#2344;"], "answer": 0, "solution_en": "<p>LCM of 8, 10, 15 and 27 = 1080 s = 18 minutes</p><p>Required time = 7:00 am + 18 minutes = 7:18 am</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>LCM of 8, 10, 15 and 27 = 1080 s = 18 minutes</p><p>Required time = 7:00 am + 18 minutes = 7:18 am</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "HCF & LCM"}, {"q_en": "<p>A shopkeeper has a certain quantity of wheat. He sold 40 kg of total wheat at 33(1/3) % profit and the rest at 20% profit. If the shopkeeper gained 28(8/9) % profit on the whole, then find the total quantity of wheat?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>&#2319;&#2325; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2375; &#2346;&#2366;&#2360; &#2344;&#2367;&#2358;&#2381;&#2330;&#2367;&#2340; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; &#2327;&#2375;&#2361;&#2370;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2404; &#2313;&#2360;&#2344;&#2375; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; 40 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379; &#2327;&#2375;&#2361;&#2370;&#2305; 33(1/3)% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2352; &#2324;&#2352; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; 20% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2346;&#2352; &#2348;&#2375;&#2330;&#2366;&#2404; &#2351;&#2342;&#2367; &#2342;&#2369;&#2325;&#2366;&#2344;&#2342;&#2366;&#2352; &#2325;&#2379; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2350;&#2367;&#2354;&#2366;&#2325;&#2352; 28(8/9)% &#2354;&#2366;&#2349; &#2361;&#2369;&#2310;, &#2340;&#2379; &#2327;&#2375;&#2361;&#2370;&#2305; &#2325;&#2368; &#2325;&#2369;&#2354; &#2350;&#2366;&#2340;&#2381;&#2352;&#2366; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2368;&#2332;&#2367;&#2319;?</p>", "options_en": ["80 kg", "60 kg", "90 kg", "40 kg"], "options_hi": ["80 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;", "60 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;", "90 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;", "40 &#2325;&#2367;&#2354;&#2379;"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>By the rule of alligation:</p><p><img width=259 height=61 id=\"Picture 24\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p9671/image003.png\"></p><p>Ratio = 2: 1</p><p>Given,</p><p>The quantity of wheat, which is sold at 33(1/3) % = 40 kg</p><p>So, the quantity of wheat, which is sold at 20% profit = 40 * &frac12; = 20 kg</p><p>So, the total quantity of wheat = 40 + 20 = 60 kg</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>By the rule of alligation:</p><p><img width=259 height=61 id=\"Picture 24\" src=\"https://u1.oliveboard.in/exams/solution/oliveimg/p9671/image003.png\"></p><p>Ratio = 2: 1</p><p>Given,</p><p>The quantity of wheat, which is sold at 33(1/3) % = 40 kg</p><p>So, the quantity of wheat, which is sold at 20% profit = 40 * &frac12; = 20 kg</p><p>So, the total quantity of wheat = 40 + 20 = 60 kg</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Ratio & Proportion"}, {"q_en": "<p>Find the value of (5<sup>1</sup>  -  5<sup>2/3</sup> + 5<sup>5/3</sup>) (5<sup>1/3</sup>  -  5<sup>4/3</sup>) + 4 * 5<sup>4/3.</sup></p>", "q_hi": "<p>(5<sup>1</sup> - 5<sup>2/3</sup> + 5<sup>5/3</sup>) (5<sup>1/3</sup> - 5<sup>4/3</sup>) + 4 * 5<sup>4/3.</sup> &#2325;&#2366; &#2350;&#2366;&#2344; &#2332;&#2381;&#2334;&#2366;&#2340; &#2325;&#2352;&#2375;&#2306;&#2404;</p>", "options_en": ["120", "-120", "80", "-80"], "options_hi": ["120", "-120", "80", "-80"], "answer": 3, "solution_en": "<p>(5<sup>1</sup>  -  5<sup>2/3</sup> + 5<sup>5/3</sup>) (5<sup>1/3</sup>  -  5<sup>4/3</sup>) + 4 * 5<sup>4/3</sup></p><p>= (5<sup>4/3</sup>  -  5 + 5<sup>2</sup>  -  5<sup>7/3</sup> + 5<sup>2</sup>  -  5<sup>3</sup>) + 4 * 5<sup>4/3</sup></p><p>= (5<sup>4/3</sup>  -  5 + 5<sup>2</sup>  -  5<sup>7/3</sup> + 5<sup>2</sup>  -  5<sup>3</sup>) + 5<sup>4/3</sup> (5<sup>1</sup>  -  1)</p><p>= (5<sup>4/3</sup>  -  5 + 5<sup>2</sup>  -  5<sup>7/3</sup> + 5<sup>2</sup>  -  5<sup>3</sup>) + 5<sup>7/3</sup>  -  5<sup>4/3</sup></p><p>=  - 5 + 5<sup>2</sup> + 5<sup>2</sup>  -  5<sup>3</sup></p><p>=  - 5 + 25 + 25  -  125</p><p>=  - 80</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>(5<sup>1</sup>  -  5<sup>2/3</sup> + 5<sup>5/3</sup>) (5<sup>1/3</sup>  -  5<sup>4/3</sup>) + 4 * 5<sup>4/3</sup></p><p>= (5<sup>4/3</sup>  -  5 + 5<sup>2</sup>  -  5<sup>7/3</sup> + 5<sup>2</sup>  -  5<sup>3</sup>) + 4 * 5<sup>4/3</sup></p><p>= (5<sup>4/3</sup>  -  5 + 5<sup>2</sup>  -  5<sup>7/3</sup> + 5<sup>2</sup>  -  5<sup>3</sup>) + 5<sup>4/3</sup> (5<sup>1</sup>  -  1)</p><p>= (5<sup>4/3</sup>  -  5 + 5<sup>2</sup>  -  5<sup>7/3</sup> + 5<sup>2</sup>  -  5<sup>3</sup>) + 5<sup>7/3</sup>  -  5<sup>4/3</sup></p><p>=  - 5 + 5<sup>2</sup> + 5<sup>2</sup>  -  5<sup>3</sup></p><p>=  - 5 + 25 + 25  -  125</p><p>=  - 80</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Mixed Practice"}, {"q_en": "<p>In a class of 50 students 20% are girls and rest are boys. Average marks of boys are 45 and that of girls are 40. What are the average marks of the whole class?</p>", "q_hi": "<p>50 &#2357;&#2367;&#2342;&#2381;&#2351;&#2366;&#2352;&#2381;&#2341;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2368; &#2319;&#2325; &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2350;&#2375;&#2306; 20% &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2366;&#2305; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2358;&#2375;&#2359; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; 45 &#2361;&#2376;&#2306; &#2324;&#2352; &#2354;&#2337;&#2364;&#2325;&#2367;&#2351;&#2379;&#2306; &#2325;&#2375; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; 40 &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;&#2404; &#2360;&#2306;&#2346;&#2370;&#2352;&#2381;&#2339; &#2325;&#2325;&#2381;&#2359;&#2366; &#2325;&#2375; &#2324;&#2360;&#2340; &#2309;&#2306;&#2325; &#2325;&#2367;&#2340;&#2344;&#2375; &#2361;&#2376;&#2306;?</p>", "options_en": ["50", "44", "38", "54"], "options_hi": ["50", "44", "38", "54"], "answer": 1, "solution_en": "<p>Number of girls = 20% of 50 = 10</p><p>Number of boys = 50  -  10 = 40</p><p>Total marks of all boys = 45 X 40 = 1800</p><p>Total marks of all girls = 40 X 10 = 400</p><p>Average marks of whole class = (1800+400)/50 = 2200/50 = 44</p>", "solution_hi": "<p>Number of girls = 20% of 50 = 10</p><p>Number of boys = 50  -  10 = 40</p><p>Total marks of all boys = 45 X 40 = 1800</p><p>Total marks of all girls = 40 X 10 = 400</p><p>Average marks of whole class = (1800+400)/50 = 2200/50 = 44</p>", "marks": 1.0, "neg": 0.25, "chap": "Average"}]}